From 843e3c9856eea5216fe28b21d9c189472418609d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:43:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rollback: write the undo journal before moving the previous
 file

With rollback: true, a CSV or Parquet output in replace mode is published by
renaming the previous file to .hydra-bak-*, then putting the new one in place.
The journal was written after that, so a hard kill in between left no journal
and an orphan backup: the next run overwrote the half-published outputs
silently. The load session now announces the move to the journal first
(push_pending); push_job replaces the entry once the load is sealed. A run
killed in between is refused at the next start and 'hdrctl workflow undo'
restores the previous files.

Replace-mode file outputs only; database outputs and append mode unchanged.
Found with the crash scenario of hydra-etl-benchmark.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011X5H6WN7YFXx8LCdr73MxR
